    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121-a1">

                <pb facs="0209" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg943"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Governor McIntire to Mr. Uhl.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Denver, Colo.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Acting Italian consul returned last night from Walsenburg. Called on me this
                    morning. Expressed himself satisfied with course of authorities there. It is
                    certain that Vittone and Ronchietto had taken out first papers. Lorenzo
                    Andinino, heretofore <pb facs="0210" n="944" xml:id="pg944"/> called Danino, is
                    probably not an American citizen, but may be. Giacobino, who escaped from first
                    attack, is safe; feet badly frosted. Gobetto is believed to be safe also. These
                    two men, as I am informed, took out first papers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert W. McIntire</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
